#: ../../source/fun_project/07-fun_Doorbell.rst:52
msgid "3. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/07-fun_Doorbell.rst:54
msgid "The main idea behind this project is to use the Arduino Uno board to detect a button press and, in response, play a melody on the passive buzzer. The melody consists of a sequence of notes (defined by their pitches) and their durations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/07-fun_Doorbell.rst:56
msgid "Setting up necessary libraries and global variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/07-fun_Doorbell.rst:69
msgid "This segment includes the necessary library for musical notes and sets up the pins for our components. Additionally, the melody and its durations are defined in arrays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/07-fun_Doorbell.rst:71
msgid "Initializing the button and starting serial communication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/07-fun_Doorbell.rst:80
msgid "In the ``setup()`` function, we start serial communication and configure the buttonPin to act as an input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/07-fun_Doorbell.rst:82
msgid "Monitoring the button press to play the melody"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/07-fun_Doorbell.rst:95
msgid "Here, we continuously check the state of the button in the loop. If pressed, a message is sent to the serial monitor, and the ``buzzer()`` function (which plays the melody) is called."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/07-fun_Doorbell.rst:97
msgid "The ``buzzer()`` function to play the melody"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/fun_project/07-fun_Doorbell.rst:114
msgid "In the ``buzzer()`` function, the melody's notes are played sequentially. The ``tone()`` function generates a tone on the buzzer for a specified duration. After playing each note, there's a brief pause before playing the next note."
msgstr ""
